WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.680
17,000 feet down in two minutes. Passengers stopped in alleged stabbing on a Tel Aviv bound flight.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:14.060
This is Omni View Africa &amp; Middle East, Episode 9. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:21.040
The Guardian reports the jet was fly Dubai Flight FZ1073, Dubai to Tel Aviv,

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:27.060
forced down in Saudi Arabia on the 30th of September after one pilot allegedly stabbed the other.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.720
There, Israeli officials say the pilot accused of that stabbing is an Omani citizen.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.620
passenger Yani of Hanyun told Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu he locked the attacker

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.040
in a chokehold and hauled him out of the cockpit.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.240
Hanyun said the man was trying to smash the instruments and disable the plane.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:50.620
The BBC names the pilot who is stabbed as Indian Captain Smith Machar and Israel's Prime

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:51.740
Minister hailed him.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:57.560
Fly Dubai says services to and from Israel stay grounded while investigators work, and

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.000
that the motive is still unclear.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:05.720
Netanyahu told CNN that Israel had word Iran's proxies were planning attacks, but no specific

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:09.720
warning on this flight, and that it is too early to say who was behind it.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:15.220
After that call, President Donald Trump said the co-pilot was perhaps a terrorist or

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.000
perhaps a whack drop, and that he stabbed the pilot.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.320
Israel's Defense Minister has called the incident a thwarted terror attack.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.300
The US State Department says four Americans were on board, and that American diplomats

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.640
in the kingdom are talking to Saudi investigators.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.160
Foreign Minister Penny Wong says at least two Australians are safe, and she thanked the

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.460
heroes who stopped the attack.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:40.660
Israel's Embassy in Australia says they are a Jewish couple from Sydney.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:46.820
Ambassador Hillel Newman called it an attempt to hit the Abraham Accords, the 2020 deal that

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:52.240
normalized relations between the UAE and Israel. Across the region, President Bolit

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.660
Tanubu used Nigeria's 66th Independence Day to say four years cannot wipe out economic

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:03.360
damage built over generations. Arise News reported. He said the hardships since the reforms

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:08.820
is real, and that he inherited an economy in deep distress. He said the emergency treatment

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:13.900
is over, and that Nigeria has entered an age of prosperity. He called people pushing a

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.760
return to petrol subsidies, influential, but regressive voices.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:25.360
Arise News puts petrol at about 195 Nira a liter when he took office in May 2023, and

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.240
around 1,500 Nira now, a rise of more than 650 percent.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:36.280
It puts the dollar at about 460 Nira then, and around 1,500 now.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:42.920
In Zimbabwe, businessman Wichnell Chavayo and his wife, Lucy Mutege, died when a helicopter

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:47.820
The helicopter came down on Wednesday evening near Morondara, about 70 kilometers east of

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.680
Harari, the BBC reported.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.680
Police say all six people on board were killed.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:57.360
Commissioner Paul Nyathy put the crash at about five in the afternoon local time.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:03.500
Government officials say two of the six were pilots, and spokesman Nick Mengwana said nobody

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.080
survived.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.340
Family spokesperson Herbert Chavio confirmed the deaths to the state broadcaster ZBC.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:15.280
ZBC says the group left Gandami in Chikamba, where the couple were building a rural home

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.380
and hit the ground at Kudanga Farm about 40 minutes after takeoff.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.720
Police say the cause is not yet known, and the investigation is open.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:29.560
Chavio ran intra-trek Zimbabwe and had denied allegations of wrongdoing over his contracts.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:36.440
Those dealings included a $172 million solar project at Kwanda, awarded by the state-owned

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:41.700
Zimbabwe power company and fought in court for years, and scrutiny of materials bought for

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:47.940
the disputed 2023 elections. Also today, Gaza's civil defense said crews pulled the bodies in

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:55.580
remains of 105 Palestinians from under a residential block in Altaj, Central Gaza City, across 17 days,

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:02.200
working with an Egyptian committee. In Ghana, former Lance Minister Samuel Abu Jnapur wants to buy

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:07.660
partisan parliamentary inquiry after French authorities seized nearly 3.9 tons of cocaine

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:12.520
in Dunkirk on the 10th of September in a container reportedly shipped from Ghana.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:17.660
Sudan's government has extended the omening of the adrey crossing for three more months.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:24.020
In Addis Ababa, a senior adviser to Sudan's army-led authorities said a United States proposal

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:28.540
for a 90-day ceasefire risks splitting Sudan the way Libya was split.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:35.400
In the wider world, more than 60 women entrepreneurs opened a two-week training course in Johannesburg on Tuesday.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.500
Grit Daily News reported, citing Xinhua.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:45.560
The course sits inside the Global Female Entrepreneurs Empowerment Program, run by Beijing Foreign Studies University.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:52.240
About 100 people from Chinese and South African business, education, and media sat in with the trainees.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:58.520
Former African Union Commission Chair in Kosozana, Dlamini, Zuma, thanked China, said

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:03.400
no country reaches its potential without women's talent, and told the room, we have to build

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.420
the Africa we want.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:10.060
Xu Jianhao, who runs China Construction Banks, Johannesburg Branch, and whose bank backed

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:14.780
the workshop, said women's economic power is growing inside China-Africa trade.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:20.940
Wei Dengze, of the South Africa-China Economic and Trade Association, invited women led

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:24.500
South African firms to look for partnerships with the association's members.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:29.800
The case on both sides today is whether Botswana should kill elephants to feed an independent

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:30.460
celebration.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:36.100
The government has authorized the killing of 23 elephants, and the hunting of Kudu, Impala,

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:41.020
and Wildebeest, so the meat can go out across eight districts for the 60th anniversary.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.020
Supporters of the hunting policies say foreign criticism misses what rural communities live

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.860
with beside huge elephant herds.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.280
Their sharpest point is damage at home.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.040
Elephants can wreck crops and property and put people in danger as settlements press

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.020
closer to wildlife.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:01.120
The government defends regulated hunting as a tool against that conflict and as a way

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.360
to raise money for communities and for conservation.

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:08.460
All Africa reports Botswana has more than 130,000 elephants.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:14.260
The elephant protection society warns that serving elephants at a national feast could weaken

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.200
conservation and encourage poaching.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:22.000
that is the case against in its strongest form. A state feast can make killing elephants look

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:27.340
acceptable. Separately, the kill has raised hygiene and disease worries during a foot and mouth

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:33.380
outbreak and local officials want the meat processed and handed out more safely. Both sides start from

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:38.960
the same act. The government approved those 23 elephants for the anniversary and the meat is meant

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:45.460
for distribution. The reporting names no court date and no reversal. What it does record next is that

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:48.660
call for safer handling, set against the society's warning.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.780
A sign of progress did not turn up in today's reporting.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:52.960
